Kernel UAPI (clean-room)
------------------------

Original pure-Zig eBPF loader / attach layer / BTF parser / event-ring
consumers, clean-room from the kernel UAPI headers (`linux/bpf.h`,
`linux/btf.h`, `linux/perf_event.h`, `linux/if_link.h`; **GPL-2.0 WITH
Linux-syscall-note**) and the kernel's own BPF and BTF documentation.

No GPL header source is copied — only the uncopyrightable ABI facts they
document are used (struct layouts, command/attribute/flag constants,
instruction encoding). The operative mechanism is the same Linux-syscall-note
exception relied on by `netlink`/`genetlink`/`wireguard`/`tc`.

Design reference
----------------

libbpf (**LGPL-2.1-or-later OR BSD-2-Clause**) — API SHAPE only, no source
ported or read while implementing. The module's `meta.model_after` has always
named it; this record states it explicitly per CONVENTIONS §5.

The following algorithm shapes are known to match libbpf's documented
behaviour and are declared so rather than left implicit: the CO-RE bitfield
load-widening and LSHIFT/RSHIFT derivation, the `btf_trace_`/`bpf_lsm_`/
`bpf_iter_` prefix conventions, `___flavor` suffix stripping in CO-RE target
matching, a bounded type-resolution depth of 32, and split-BTF detection via
the base string section's leading NUL. Each was derived from the UAPI
semantics and verified empirically against this machine's real
`/sys/kernel/btf/vmlinux` (cross-checked with `bpftool btf dump ... format
raw`) and against genuine `clang -target bpf -O2 -g` output.
